## Context

2026-11-09, MeSSH slides deposit (hal-05858144): the agent ran the
pre-upload PDF review, the payload gate and the X-test dry run, then the
real POST, and only afterwards, on the author's question « t'es sûr que
c'est pas déjà déposé en une autre version ? », searched HAL, the mail
archive, the project and the homepage bib for an earlier deposit. None
existed, but the order was wrong: a second POST creates a duplicate
record that only a moderator can merge, and the skill's own § 2c says so
without asking for the search that would prevent it.

## Design

Add a step 2a-0 « Prior record check » to `skills/update-publist/SKILL.md`,
before the TEI is built, with its own GATE line:

- Public HAL search by author and title words
  (`authIdHal_s:minh-ha-duong AND title_t:(...)`), and by the companion
  work's `seeAlso` when the deposit is a slide deck or a translation.
- The private side the public API does not show: `Ha-Duong.bib` for an
  `eprint` on the same object or its companion, the project's STATE.md,
  the dated `release/` folders of the object, the mail archive for a HAL
  acknowledgement carrying the title (the `email` skill's paths).
- Outcome written in the release record: `prior_deposit_check` with
  what was searched and what was found. A hit routes to `PUT
  /sword/hal/{id}` (new version) or to the author, never to a POST.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] SKILL.md carries the step and its gate, before 2a
- [ ] The release record template names `prior_deposit_check`
- [ ] Hygiene tests pass

## Imagine (raid 681f31, 2026-11-09)

Premise holds: no commit on `skills/update-publist/` since the ticket was
created; open PR #2318 is ticket-only. Reimagine (Sonnet 5.5) and Blind-Spot
pass (Opus 5.5, three material findings, folded in below).

- **Placement.** One new `### Prior record check (GATE)` section directly
  after the Step 2 credentials preamble, before « Pre-upload PDF review »:
  cheapest check, independent of the PDF, and it satisfies « before 2a ».
  The ticket's « 2a-0 » label is kept only in the section's first line
  (« step 2a-0 of this skill ») so the exit criterion reads literally.
- **No script, no test, no helper.** A checklist in prose is proportionate.
- **The release record template is the release-journal entry** of the
  paper runbooks (`skills/paper/references/submitted.md:21`, `resubmitted.md:20`,
  `accepted.md:21`: « naming the platform, the files uploaded, the deposits and
  the tag »), through which every HAL deposit is routed with
  `/update-publist --hal-only`. No other template exists in this repository
  and no `email` skill exists. Criterion 2 is met by (a) defining the
  `prior_deposit_check` block (searched, found, route: none|PUT|author) in the
  new step and (b) adding `prior_deposit_check` to those three release-journal
  lines. The mail archive is named as « the author's mail archive, with
  whichever mail tool the session has », no invented paths.
- **The common duplicate is a new version with a stale hal-id**, not a
  fresh object (§ 2d already says so). A hit yields the `{hal-id}` that § 2c's
  PUT needs; when the bib `eprint`, STATE.md and HAL disagree, the author
  decides.
- **A record under moderation is invisible to the public search API.** A
  SWORD POST made in this session or in the last days counts as a hit until
  HAL's mail confirms it. Named limitation: a deposit under another idHal is
  not caught.
- **Query syntax verified** on the public API
  (`authIdHal_s:minh-ha-duong AND title_t:(w1 OR w2)`); use distinctive
  title words joined by OR. `seeAlso` is not a search field: the companion
  work is searched by its title or halId.
- **Review point.** Next `/update-publist` run or ~60 days: does the
  transcript or release-journal entry carry `prior_deposit_check` before the
  first POST? No run by then: drop the review.

Drift guard: criteria 1 to 3 kept; the runbook lines are the template
criterion 2 names, not new scope.

## Plan (raid 681f31)

Prose only; no script, no new test file. Four files.

### Actions

1. `skills/update-publist/SKILL.md`: insert `### Prior record check (GATE)`
   between the Step 2 credentials preamble (line 96, « Mask `<hal:password>` … »)
   and `### Pre-upload PDF review (GATE)` (line 98). Content, in this order:
   - one line: this is step 2a-0 of the skill; it runs before any TEI is
     built and before the PDF review, because a hit changes the whole route;
   - public HAL: one `curl` GET on the search API with
     `q=authIdHal_s:minh-ha-duong AND title_t:(w1 OR w2)`, distinctive title
     words joined by OR, `fl=halId_s,title_s,docType_s,version_i`; for a
     slide deck or translation, a second search on the companion work's
     title or halId;
   - private side: `~/CNRS/html/src/Ha-Duong.bib` (`eprint` on the object or
     its companion), the project's `STATE.md`, its dated `release/` folders,
     the author's mail archive for a HAL acknowledgement carrying the title,
     with whichever mail tool the session has;
   - a SWORD POST made in this session or in the last days counts as a hit
     until HAL's mail confirms it (a record under moderation is not in the
     public API); a deposit under another idHal is not caught;
   - the record block, verbatim shape:
     `prior_deposit_check: searched=[…] found=[hal-id|none] route=none|PUT|author`,
     shown to the author;
   - **GATE** line: a hit yields the `{hal-id}` for § 2c's PUT, never a POST;
     sources that disagree go to the author; `none` allows 2a. No TEI before
     this block is shown.
2. Same file, § 2c « Updating an existing deposit » (line 224): add that the
   `{hal-id}` is the one the Prior record check found.
3. `skills/paper/references/submitted.md:21-22`, `resubmitted.md:20`,
   `accepted.md:21`: the release-journal entry also names
   `prior_deposit_check` (the block of update-publist's step 2a-0).
   `published.md` has no release-journal line and is left alone.

### First test

No red test exists for prose. Evidence instead, quoted in the merge request:
- `grep -n "Prior record check\|### 2a\." skills/update-publist/SKILL.md`
  shows the gate heading before the 2a heading;
- `grep -rn prior_deposit_check skills/` hits the four files;
- `python3 scripts/scoped-check.py` (doc-only diff) with `selected:` and
  `skipped:` quoted, then `make check-fast` green.

### Dependencies

None. PR #2318 (ticket 1484, model-invocation flag) touches no shared line.

